  "why": "Cabanes-Späth proves the statement for every finite group and every prime (Theorem A), which is the whole question; its first written argument is the 27 Oct 2024 arXiv posting (Annals received it 31 Jul 2024, also after the snapshot), so the Oct 2023 talks do not move it before 26 Jan 2024. Annals of Mathematics, a journal of record, accepted it after refereeing, which is digestion; the Quanta comments are only praise. No AI is credited. The earlier p = 2 and p = 3 results are cases, digested by Annals/Inventiones, and fall before the snapshot. The IMN reduction and the simple-group inductive-condition papers are steps toward a proof, not cases of the statement, so they score none. The Galois, Alperin-McKay, sum-of-squares, bijection, equivariant and sporadic refinements are variants. Rossi 2026 used AI on a different conjecture and its systems list is empty, so it scores none and earns nothing for this problem. The Lean item is a statement with sorry and no date.",
